# Broker access rules. Copy to secrets/mqtt.acl and adapt.
#
# One identity per field node, and a node reaches only its own namespace: it writes
# its telemetry and health (its MQTT last will is a health message) and reads its own
# commands. It can not read another node's data.
# Replace NODE_ID per device; repeat the block for every node.
user field-node-NODE_ID
topic write armor/node/NODE_ID/telemetry
topic write armor/node/NODE_ID/health
# Where the node's own web panel is (its address), for a console to link to.
topic write armor/node/NODE_ID/info
topic read armor/node/NODE_ID/command
# The pins mapped in the node's web panel are devices named after the node (armor/device/NODE_ID/<pin>/state and /set).
topic readwrite armor/device/NODE_ID/#

# The central service observes every node and is the only one allowed to send commands.
user armor-server
topic read armor/node/+/telemetry
topic read armor/node/+/health
topic read armor/node/+/info
# What the solar gateway nodes and the electrical nodes measure (each node writes only its own subtree, see scripts/mqtt_identity.sh).
topic read armor/solar/#
topic read armor/electrical/#
topic write armor/node/+/command
# Alarm output: the server publishes alert.raised / alert.cleared / node.offline / node.stale here.
topic write armor/server/alert
# Smart devices (smoke, door, plug, light ...): the server listens on their state and commands them.
topic readwrite armor/device/#

# An electrical node (ARMOR-ELECTRICAL, scripts/mqtt_identity.sh add electrical-node ID): it writes what it measures and its answers, and reads nothing.
# user electrical-node-electrical-1
# topic write armor/electrical/electrical-1/state
# topic write armor/electrical/electrical-1/result
#
# A command to a node's switch is refused by the broker unless BOTH of these lines exist, and only `scripts/mqtt_identity.sh electrical-switching ID on` writes them
# (`off` removes them). The server also needs ARMOR_ELECTRICAL_SWITCHING=1 and the node has to allow switching itself: three independent switches, all off by default.
#   in the block of electrical-node-electrical-1:   topic read armor/electrical/electrical-1/command
#   in the block of armor-server:                   topic write armor/electrical/electrical-1/command

# An alarm consumer (a siren controller, a notifier) only reads alerts.
# user alarm-consumer
# topic read armor/server/alert

# One smart device that speaks MQTT itself (a Tasmota plug, an ESP32 sensor) reaches only its own topics.
# user device-kitchen
# topic readwrite armor/device/kitchen/#

# A bridge to many devices (Zigbee2MQTT with base_topic armor/device, a Shelly gateway) needs all of them.
# user bridge-zigbee
# topic readwrite armor/device/#
